{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-brings-is-qou","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:brings-is-qou","kind":"proposition","title":"Bring's surface is a quantum observable universe","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-qu-to-qou"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-brings-is-qou"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Brings.brings_is_qou","text":"brings-is-qou.md","leanSource":"brings-is-qou.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:brings-is-qou\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Bring's surface is a quantum observable universe</em></p>\n<p>Bring's surface <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma_4</code> (<a href=\"#def:brings-surface\">Bring's surface</a>) determines a quantum observable universe over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> (with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">30 \\in R^{\\times}</code>).</p>\n"}
